	"description": [
		"This seminar designed for majors examines secession and the southern rebellion, especially their relationship to slavery and racial violence. Topics include society during wartime, gender and the home front, what happened on the battlefield and the coming of emancipation. The course concludes with an examination of the modern debates over the Confederate legacy, including the controversy over Confederate statues at places like Charlottesville and Richmond."
